<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- The SDK here is a .NET 11 preview, whose F# compiler defaults to language
         version 11. Ionide 7.31.1 carries an older compiler service that rejects that
         value outright and then fails every typecheck, so the editor has no IntelliSense
         at all while the command line builds perfectly well.

         Naming the language version explicitly keeps the preview SDK and gives the
         editor a value it can parse. Raise it when Ionide ships a compiler service that
         knows 11.

         (No double hyphen in this comment: MSBuild parses the file as XML, where two of
         them is a parse error. Compiler flags written out in prose are the easiest way
         to introduce one by accident, which is how this comment first failed.) -->
    <LangVersion>10.0</LangVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
